# Accepted gaps for 68-decorator-framework-roots — each line is an edge the TypeScript
# compiler resolves and this engine does not. A NEW missing edge fails the suite;
# a line here that STARTS working also fails, so the debt cannot rot.
#
# All five are one gap, tracked as #233: a decorator FACTORY is called and gets its
# edge (call_kind DECORATOR_CALL), but the function that factory RETURNS is then
# applied to the decorated declaration, and that second hop has no call site. The
# compiler sees it, so every legacy decorator in this ecosystem loses one edge.
#
# This case does not depend on the gap. The roots it exists to test are derived from
# the decorator's NAME through annotation_on, never from the application edge, which
# is why they are correct while these five are still absent. When #233 lands, these
# lines start working and this file must be emptied in the same commit.
OrderController#add(string) -> container#<arrow@13>(object,string,PropertyDescriptor)
OrderController#getOne(string) -> container#<arrow@12>(object,string,PropertyDescriptor)
container#<module-init>() -> container#<arrow@10>(Function)
container#<module-init>() -> container#<arrow@11>(Function)
container#<module-init>() -> container#<arrow@9>(Function)
